WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:05.920
Even before landing the lead in Bohemian Rhapsody,
Rami Malek was an accomplished talent, and

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:11.090
he's made an impression over the last decade
as one of Hollywood's most intriguing young

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:11.580
stars.

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:15.700
Here are the biggest reasons why the actor
who plays Freddie Mercury looks so familiar.

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:21.940
Like pretty much every actor who went to Hollywood
with dreams of making it big, Rami Malek started

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:22.440
small.

00:00:22.949 --> 00:00:28.339
His first ever on-screen role was as an enthusiastic
bible study participant on Gilmore Girls in

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:33.260
2004, which he followed up with one-off stints
on Medium, Alcatraz, and Believe.

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:39.720
"My name is Rami Malek, and welcome to GQ
Middle East.”

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:44.880
And because of his Egyptian background, Malek
was often cast as Middle Eastern characters

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:49.640
in series like the Iraq War FX drama Over
There, and Fox's 24.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:54.420
If you were a kid in the mid-2000s, the reason
Malek looks familiar is because he starred

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:57.740
in one of the most popular family film franchises
of all time.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:02.300
In the three A Night at the Museum movies,
Ben Stiller played an unassuming night watchman

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:06.680
at the American Museum of Natural History
in New York City… where the historical figures

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:08.200
in the exhibits come to life.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:12.600
Among them, is a pharaoh from ancient Egypt
- portrayed by Malek.

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:16.000
"My parents gave me this tablet 3,000 years
ago.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.340
It has a magical power that brings all of
the exhibits to life.”

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:20.700
No really.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:21.460
What's it do?”

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:26.840
The guy who would one day play Freddie Mercury
under plenty of makeup and prosthetics is

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:31.400
still recognizable, only here he acts from
underneath traditional Egyptian garb.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:36.780
Before his Emmy-winning, star-making work
on Mr. Robot, Malek's initial TV breakthrough

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:42.120
was a major role in HBO's Emmy-winning miniseries,
The Pacific, in 2010.

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:47.070
Not only was the story based on real events
during World War II, but Malek's character,

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:50.540
Private First Class Shelton, was based on
a real person, as well.

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:55.600
In a roundtable discussion in 2016, Malek
credited the role with preparing him to play

00:01:55.600 --> 00:02:00.350
more complex people, without internalizing
the emotional baggage of the character.

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:07.150
“And taking that home every day… it physically
and psychologically really had kind of a negative

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:08.140
impact on me.”

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:14.660
Malek broke out for good in 2015 when he landed
the lead role of Elliot Anderson on Mr. Robot.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:18.020
"I started intercepting all the traffic on
your network.

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:19.000
I decided to hack you.”

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:20.680
“Are you blackmailing me?”

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:23.680
“I don't give a s--- about money.”

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:30.220
The ambitious, mysterious, and unpredictable
USA series concerns the exploits of genius

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:34.620
hacker, Elliot - who has a split personality
disorder and can't always decipher what's

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:35.580
real and what isn't.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:40.820
The complicated role not only made Malek a
star, it earned him an Emmy for Outstanding

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:43.400
Lead Actor in a Dramatic Series, in 2016.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:50.700
The brutal original 1973 film, Papillon, starred
Steve McQueen as a real-life early-20th century

00:02:50.719 --> 00:02:55.249
criminal-turned South American penal colony
resident, best-known by his nickname - a.k.a.,

00:02:55.249 --> 00:02:58.919
the title of the movie - Papillon, which means
"butterfly".

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:02.640
"You double-cross me, I'll kill you.”

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:08.420
And in 2017, Papillon got the Hollywood remake
treatment, with Charlie Hunnam as the lead,

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:11.260
while Malek played the thoughtful and crafty
Dega.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:14.480
"You seem like the kind of man who can make
up his own mind.”

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:17.100
“You're a good judge of character.”

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:22.559
The film earned a small theatrical release
in North America, but established Malek as

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:25.100
a movie star, not just a TV actor.

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:30.900
Part of what makes Mr. Robot so intriguing
is Malek's in-character narration as the troubled

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:31.900
Elliot Alderson.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:33.920
"Just a regular cyber-security engineer.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:37.079
But I'm a vigilante hacker by night.”

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:41.879
But the actor has been honing his voice acting
skills throughout his entire decade-and-a-half

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:42.380
career.

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:47.459
One of his first acting jobs was recording
dialogue for a variety of minor characters

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.760
in the classic video game Halo 2.

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:55.680
He also had a run on Nickelodeon's beloved
fantasy series The Legend of Korra as Tahno,

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:58.860
a role he reprised in a video game adaptation
of the show.

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:02.580
"This is going to be a sensational season
of television.”

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:07.819
Notably, Malek's BoJack Horseman character,
Flip McVicker, a quirky filmmaker, enjoyed

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:11.629
a major plot arc in the fourth and fifth season
of the Netflix series.

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:15.959
"Is all of this a tooty-fruity illusion covered
in sprinkles?

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:19.060
So, so, so many sprinkles."

